cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or the associated derived data, please cite both
  the archived release (this file) and the manuscript / preprint listed
  under preferred-citation.
type: software
title: >-
  Python Scripts, Jupyter Notebooks, and Results for "Weddell-Ross
  Snow-Thickness Contrast over Antarctic Sea Ice from Multi-Winter CRYO2ICE
  Observations"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-05-28"
license: MIT
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/xinlongliu0307/cryo2ice-antarctic-snow-depth
url: https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.19220192
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.19220192
abstract: >-
  Complete processing pipeline used to retrieve Antarctic snow thickness from
  coincident ICESat-2 ATL10 V7 and CryoSat-2 Baseline-E (L2E) observations
  over the CRYO2ICE period (August 2022 - September 2025), together with the
  Jupyter notebooks that generate the manuscript figures, tables, and
  sensitivity-test outputs (delta sensitivity 0.30-0.90, SIC threshold
  50-90 %, collocation radius 3.5/5.0/7.0 km), gridding onto the 6.25 km
  NSIDC polar stereographic South grid, and AMSR2 inter-comparison.

